{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Clarifying the review advisory on 'one module-level pytest.mark.skipif per module': the implementation defines one module-level marker object (_POSIX_SHELL_SUBJECT) per module and applies it per test, only to the listed POSIX-subject tests. No module is skipped wholesale; e.g. the ported seatbelt test in test_mutation_sandbox.py is unmarked (commit d8b1aec2633)."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1795258191617790001,"uuid":"faf5ec2f-21d9-4ac6-a55a-ad4588987d5e"}